{"agent":"bg34","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_repeat_of_terminated` assumes each element of `_review_runs(it, gate)` has an `.evidence` attribute, but the review records in this file are dictionary-like: the existing code accesses the previous run with `_last_review(it, gate)` and `last.get(\"reviewed_head\")`. For any gate with at least one prior run, a command like `ddflow review --gate critic --force --reason` enters the explicit-work branch, calls `_repeat_of_terminated`, and executes `runs[-1].evidence`; if the stored records are dicts, this raises `AttributeError: 'dict' object has no attribute 'evidence'` before a reviewer can run. It should read `runs[-1].get(\"evidence\")`.","digest":"a79b41080f25a0e8","location":"ddflow/api/review/scope.py:_repeat_of_terminated","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/review/scope.py:_repeat_of_terminated"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The fixture `_setup` deliberately makes the fake reviewer return `STATUS: FINDINGS 1` by writing `x.py` containing `# FINDME`, and ddflow maps `STATUS: FINDINGS 1` to exit code `FAIL` (1). So for the exact input this test creates, `api.review` returns `out.exit == FAIL`, not `OK`, and `assert out.exit == OK` fails before the test ever checks the repeat text. The regression test cannot pass on correct code.","digest":"13fe3333230771aa","location":"tests/test_review_force_after_interrupt.py:83","severity":"HIGH","title":"tests/test_review_force_after_interrupt.py:83"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"In `ddflow/api/review/scope.py`, the function `_repeat_of_terminated(it, gate: str)` assumes `it` is an object that implements a `_review_runs(it, gate)` function or method, but `_review_runs` is called as a global function (or module-level function) which is neither imported nor defined in `scope.py`, leading to a `NameError: name '_review_runs' is not defined` when `api.review` evaluates scope rules with `force=True`. Given a repository where a review is forced after a terminated run, calling `api.review(..., force=True)` crashes immediately with a `NameError`.","digest":"94625a2aa60a541f","location":"ddflow/api/review/scope.py:_repeat_of_terminated","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/review/scope.py:_repeat_of_terminated"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":6543,"diff_sha":"f094de64273f20943d0e3e7b82006c72470e3a0be9d04bfa8b449471cd8d52d5","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1.8,"family":"deepseek","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"585457a273f760c5","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-ddflow-review-force-duplicate-round.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261107T145054Z-e6656d34.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794062667.5061154,"family":"moonshot","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"kimi-for-coding-highspeed","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"kimi-k3"}],"review_id":"023551c39253","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"c6552723334cf920ebb9bea4fd4e2dffb0f6caab","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/review/gate.py":"100644 b7578d7a3d89f96c886ff026c61d9a45a2986314","ddflow/api/review/scope.py":"100644 60031dd4ab045ca84d2fb9edbb5f940f6d611660","tests/test_review_force_after_interrupt.py":"100644 f01addb35f81dc7464c5dc4d6cc6a854eaf8b691"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","reviewer_families":["deepseek","google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/review/scope.py:_repeat_of_terminated","tests/test_review_force_after_interrupt.py:83","ddflow/api/review/scope.py:_repeat_of_terminated"],"tree_sha":"c6552723334c+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"3 finding(s)"},"id":"e0159e40bf7250913010eb231","kind":"gate.failed","